## POSITION TYPE
**Type B: Multi-driver platform thesis**

Amprius has multiple independent demand drivers: (1) defense/UAS market driven by DoD funding and NDAA compliance tailwinds, (2) commercial drone/ISR market driven by BVLOS regulatory unlocks and private sector adoption, (3) light electric vehicle market with separate design-in cycles, and (4) high-altitude platform systems as an emerging vertical. Impairment of one driver (e.g., government shutdown slowing defense procurement) does not impair the others (e.g., commercial UAS, LEV). The SiCore platform serves all four verticals from a shared manufacturing base, making this a genuine multi-driver platform thesis rather than a single-market bet.

**Fixed cap: 50%. Profit-take rule at 25% gain binds first.**

