## POSITION SIZING RECOMMENDATION
**Recommended maximum position size: 18%**

The thesis is strengthening with no stumble, Type B classification, and a strong mitigation argument — all of which support sizing toward the cap. However, three factors warrant sizing below the 50% hard cap: (1) the company is pre-profitability with negative operating cash flow ($9.2 million used in Q3), requiring continued ATM dilution; (2) the backlog-to-revenue conversion is supply-constrained, not demand-constrained, introducing execution risk on fulfillment; and (3) the Colorado facility decision remains unresolved, creating strategic optionality uncertainty. At $73.2 million cash and no debt, the balance sheet is not a near-term concern, but the dilution cadence ($25.9 million ATM in Q3 alone) is a structural drag on per-share value. 18% reflects high conviction on thesis direction while respecting the pre-profitability risk profile.

