**Fresh money allocation: 12%**

The gap between 12% (fresh money) and 18% (recommended maximum for existing holders) reflects two factors: (1) an existing holder has already absorbed the qualification risk and early-stage dilution; a fresh buyer enters at a higher valuation relative to the pre-profitability cash burn profile; and (2) the ATM offering program ($20.1 million remaining) creates near-term dilution overhang that a fresh buyer should price in. The gap is not large enough to suggest the existing position is being held on inertia — the thesis is genuinely strengthening — but it is real enough to warrant a more conservative entry for new capital. This is conviction-based holding with a modest entry discount for fresh money, not inertia.

